note top of TracingConfigurationAuthorityGuard
  Startup gate before writers.
  @AutoConfigureBefore:
  PrivateJmx, PolicyControl, ConfigServer.
  Collaborators from bootstrap
  (outside control package).
end note

' =============================================================================
' Relationships — external consumers / Agent
' =============================================================================

TracingControlMvcController --> TracingPolicyMutationService
TracingControlWebFluxManagementContextConfiguration --> TracingPolicyMutationService
TracingStatusAssembler --> AcceptedTracingPolicyReader

PrivateJmxTracingPolicySnapshotClient -[#33691F]-> AgentWriter : JMX invoke\napplySnapshot /\nreadAcceptedComplete
AgentWriter -[#33691F]-> PrivateJmxTracingPolicySnapshotClient : CompositeData response

note bottom of PrivateJmxTracingPolicySnapshotClient
  **Sole production implementor** of
  TracingPolicySnapshotApplier +
  CompleteTracingPolicyReader +
  AcceptedTracingPolicyReader.
  Encodes ExpectedTracingPolicyBase only
  from the caller's observed pair; no
  mutable identity side channel.
  STALE returned as-is (no client retry).
end note

note bottom of TracingPolicyMutationService
  Read → mutate with* → apply.
  Passes accepted.expectedBase() atomically.
  IllegalArgumentException on candidate → REJECTED.
  No Actuator retry/rebase.
end note

note bottom of TracingPolicyRefreshCoalescer
  Coalesced EnvironmentChangeEvent.
  Caches ExpectedTracingPolicyBase.
  One bounded STALE retry after
  authoritative currentComplete() reread.
  Source = CONFIG_SERVER.
end note

legend right
  |= Stereotype |= Meaning |
  | <<immutable>> | Value object; with* copy |
  | <<record>> | Java record |
  | <<exception>> | RuntimeException subtype |
  | <<AutoConfiguration>> | Spring Boot auto-config |
  | <<package-private>> | Not public API |
  | solid --> | field / constructor dependency |
  | ..|> | implements |
  | ..> | uses / throws / returns |
  | *--> | composition (record component) |
endlegend

@enduml
